      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking potassium supplements with lisinopril can be dangerous—it can spike your potassium to life-threatening levels, since lisinopril already raises potassium. The cramps are actually a common side effect of the drug, often from electrolyte shifts, not necessarily a deficiency. Please do not self-supplement; instead, call your prescriber and ask for a blood test to check your potassium levels. If you want to try something, drink a glass of pickle juice for the cramps—it’s a safe, quick fix—but get medical advice before adding any pills.",
